WEBVTT

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:04.580
And will you be purchasing that?

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:05.780
I couldn't!

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:10.750
Anyway... it doesn't really suit me.

00:00:13.390 --> 00:00:16.600
So I found a really mysterious 
tool in the pottery studio.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:19.550
It was kept far away from 
the all other tools,

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:21.440
which made it super-duper suspicious.

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:23.440
Please solve the mystery, President-san!

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:26.720
All right! Our senpai 
will solve this mystery.

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:27.710
What?!

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:29.870
Why don't we just take a look at it?

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:32.140
Sure...

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:09.480
<b>The Pottery Club of Endless Mysteries</b>

00:02:06.310 --> 00:02:07.900
Permission for a visitor?

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:09.760
Of course I got it.

00:02:09.970 --> 00:02:11.520
Perfect prep.

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:12.700
When did you do that?

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:14.700
I'm really surprised.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:17.990
Hime-chan has been proactive since 
the day we went to the outlet.

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:20.060
Hello!

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:22.270
Welcome!

00:02:22.270 --> 00:02:25.750
Sorry, we had so many customers today.

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:29.660
It was really hard for me to sneak it out.

00:02:30.430 --> 00:02:31.590
Come on in!

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:35.600
So this is your workshop.

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:42.600
It's amazing! It feels a lot like our workshop.

00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:49.360
What is this?

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:53.450
Oh, I was going to use 
that, so I set it out...

00:02:53.450 --> 00:02:54.370
Wow!

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:57.100
This is also a mystery!

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:59.150
What are these? There are so many different kinds!

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:02.880
They haven't let me see tools like these yet.

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:04.410
They said it's too soon.

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:06.410
I'm so excited!

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:08.070
¡Dios mío!

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:09.840
¡Muchas gracias!

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:11.800
Ximena-san is so cute.

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:14.870
I'll teach you what this is for.

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:16.620
So, first, this here is...

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:18.780
Hmm, that there is?

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:20.950
This is...

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:22.630
What was it again?

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:23.680
You don't know?!

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:25.940
Touko-senpai...

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:28.840
I've never seen one of those before, either.

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:31.160
What is it, Touko-senpai?

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:33.460
What, indeed?

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:35.700
How about we make it a quiz?

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:41.200
Good idea! But a quiz isn't something 
you'd normally suggest.

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:42.870
I-I wouldn't?

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:44.200
You're right...

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.490
I can see Kukuri-chan suggesting 
something like that...

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:48.590
Grandpa!

00:03:48.590 --> 00:03:50.080
What is this?

00:03:50.990 --> 00:03:53.320
Oh, this?

00:03:55.970 --> 00:03:57.690
What do you think it is?

00:03:57.690 --> 00:03:59.220
How about we make it a quiz?

00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:01.520
A quiz?

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:03.600
If you don't get it, I'll give you hints.

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:06.210
So just try to think what it could be.

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:13.860
"What is this?" "This is strange."

00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:17.850
"This is fun." 
Those are important feelings.

00:04:17.850 --> 00:04:21.000
Okay, so do you put an acorn in there?

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:22.030
Or...

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:27.820
If you don't get it, I'll give you hints.

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:30.130
So just try to think what it could be.

00:04:30.550 --> 00:04:33.900
"What is this?" "This is strange."

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:36.650
"This is fun." 
Those are important feelings.

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:38.120
Let's do this!

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:42.430
Then question one, what is this?

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:45.920
Ahh, I feel like I've seen 
one of these before.

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:48.100
What was this again?

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:49.430
It looks like a scale,

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:53.860
but this part moves and it can be 
tightened here, so that can't be it.

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:58.580
A hint: it is often used together with this.

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:05.330
Me!

00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:06.440
Yes, Naruse-san?

00:05:06.690 --> 00:05:10.270
This is a tool you use to relieve stress!

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:11.520
Incorrect.

00:05:12.070 --> 00:05:16.280
The correct answer is you use this 
to measure the outer diameter,

00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:17.770
and then use this to...

00:05:17.770 --> 00:05:20.120
Oh, to make sure the height is right!

00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:21.450
Ding ding!

00:05:21.640 --> 00:05:23.040
That's correct.

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:27.900
You use this tool when you want to make 
a lot of identically shaped pieces.

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:30.210
It's a pot gauge and a pair of calipers.

00:05:30.820 --> 00:05:32.290
I see!

00:05:32.290 --> 00:05:35.900
With these, you can make a bunch 
of identical items by hand.

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:40.630
Your "ding ding" was the best part, though.

00:05:40.630 --> 00:05:42.090
Yup, it was!

00:05:42.090 --> 00:05:42.900
Why, though?

00:05:43.310 --> 00:05:46.530
I-Isn't that the normal noise for a quiz show?

00:05:46.530 --> 00:05:49.360
It's not though, that was above and beyond!

00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:52.670
All right, sensei, what's our next question?

00:05:52.670 --> 00:05:54.520
S-Sensei?

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:57.830
I guess I am. Well, the next question is...

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:00.620
What do you think these are?

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:04.310
Oh yes, these! They look like scissors.

00:06:04.310 --> 00:06:06.120
You're right, they are scissors.

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:08.110
And when do we use them?

00:06:08.850 --> 00:06:12.630
Hmm, well you can't cut paper with them.

00:06:12.630 --> 00:06:14.940
This time, I know the answer.

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:16.600
Right, Hime-chan?

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:17.670
Yup!

00:06:17.670 --> 00:06:21.640
They come in many forms, but they're 
all used for the same thing.

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:22.970
Me!

00:06:22.970 --> 00:06:24.280
Yes, Naruse-san?

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:28.460
You use this tool to punish Kukuri-chan 
when she's being too loud.

00:06:28.460 --> 00:06:30.290
I think not!

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:32.050
Then here's a hint.

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:33.780
How do you address another person in English?

00:06:34.230 --> 00:06:35.190
"You"?

00:06:36.570 --> 00:06:39.120
I'm impressed you knew that.

00:06:40.110 --> 00:06:41.680
Very good! Very good!

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:44.750
That "you" is a big hint.

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:48.350
What comes to mind with "you" in ceramics?

00:06:56.510 --> 00:06:58.030
Could it be...

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:04.230
Do you use it like this to put the 
pieces into the yuuyaku, or glaze?

00:07:04.470 --> 00:07:05.910
Ding ding!

00:07:05.910 --> 00:07:08.100
These are glaze tongs.

00:07:08.390 --> 00:07:10.250
Glaze tongs?

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:11.930
You can use them like this...

00:07:11.930 --> 00:07:12.870
Or this!

00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:15.280
They're like robot arms!

00:07:16.150 --> 00:07:18.610
So, what do you think this is?

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:23.240
Bookend looking things 
that are not book ends!

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:26.260
Mika-chan has used these before.

00:07:26.260 --> 00:07:28.470
Huh? Really?

00:07:28.470 --> 00:07:31.430
A hint: you use them wet.

00:07:37.320 --> 00:07:38.760
I don't know, but...

00:07:40.540 --> 00:07:43.010
Maybe you use it to go like 
this... and then like this?

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:45.140
Ding ding!

00:07:45.140 --> 00:07:46.520
That's exactly it!

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:49.280
First, you get them wet.

00:07:49.930 --> 00:07:51.770
Then you clip them around 
your piece like this

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:54.660
and then lift and carry.

00:07:55.050 --> 00:07:57.890
It's a foreign tool called a "pot lift."

00:07:57.890 --> 00:07:59.300
Wow!

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:01.020
You did a good job figuring it out.

00:08:01.020 --> 00:08:04.160
Well, I just remember when I made 
bowls on the pottery wheel,

00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:07.440
I didn't like leaving fingerprints 
when picking them up,

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:11.370
so I thought having something
 like this would be nice.

00:08:11.370 --> 00:08:12.290
That's right!

00:08:12.290 --> 00:08:14.720
That's exactly what this tool is for.

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:16.550
I see.

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:20.480
It's not used often in Japan,
 but it is a very useful tool.

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:27.480
<b>Sweet Chestnuts</b>

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:31.330
Eating candy after you use your 
brain is simply the best.

00:08:31.330 --> 00:08:32.490
It's good, huh?

00:08:33.310 --> 00:08:37.000
So speaking of, what do you use this for?

00:08:38.140 --> 00:08:40.760
The very first mystery tool!

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:43.280
Right. So what do you think that is?

00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:44.310
Me, me!

00:08:44.310 --> 00:08:45.210
Naruse-san?

00:08:45.210 --> 00:08:46.010
Here we go again.

00:08:46.530 --> 00:08:49.030
When Kurikuri-chan is being loud again...

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:52.760
<b>Ninja</b>

00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:54.000
You use this foldable dart 
blower to gently punish her.

00:08:54.250 --> 00:08:55.470
Just kidding.

00:08:55.470 --> 00:08:57.270
Naruse-san!

00:08:57.270 --> 00:08:58.140
Close!

00:08:58.690 --> 00:09:00.020
It is?!

00:09:00.020 --> 00:09:02.810
So am I getting punished?

00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:06.270
No, not that. The blowing part.

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:09.610
Oh, so is this also for glazing?

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:11.020
Ding ding!

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:16.140
When people think of Mino ware, they usually 
think of ceramics like Shino or Oribe,

00:09:16.140 --> 00:09:20.170
but during the Meiji era, 
around the end of the 1800s,

00:09:20.170 --> 00:09:23.260
porcelain became very popular.

00:09:24.130 --> 00:09:26.230
These white ones, right?

00:09:26.230 --> 00:09:28.360
Oh, porcelain!

00:09:28.360 --> 00:09:32.980
But at that time, it was only considered 
as cheap, everyday stuff...

00:09:33.550 --> 00:09:34.940
Found it.

00:09:34.940 --> 00:09:40.770
That's why, to change that image into 
something with a worldwide appeal,

00:09:40.770 --> 00:09:45.820
they began to make expensive porcelain with 
finely detailed decoration and designs.

00:09:45.820 --> 00:09:48.250
And the result was Nishiura ware.

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:50.200
Wow, that's so pretty!

00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:55.270
So if you want to put light gradation on,
 like with this pot, you use this tool.

00:09:55.710 --> 00:09:57.960
A simplified sprayer.

00:09:57.960 --> 00:10:01.750
So that's a sprayer? 
How do you use it, though?

00:10:01.750 --> 00:10:02.970
Well...

00:10:03.960 --> 00:10:07.280
You put one end into the glaze,
 and then hold it like this...

00:10:11.790 --> 00:10:17.840
Then you blow into it gently and
 it produces a light, gentle color.

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:21.440
I'm glad that went well.

00:10:21.440 --> 00:10:22.510
Wow!

00:10:22.510 --> 00:10:23.990
¡Maravillosa!

00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:25.430
¡Muchas gracias!

00:10:25.430 --> 00:10:27.840
President-san, you're like the sun.

00:10:28.580 --> 00:10:29.570
I-I am?

00:10:29.570 --> 00:10:34.350
¡Sí! You're in the center of all, 
shining gently and warmly on everyone!

00:10:35.740 --> 00:10:38.660
Nobody's ever said that before.

00:10:39.050 --> 00:10:41.860
If anything, I tend to be very quiet.

00:10:41.860 --> 00:10:45.460
Yeah, I always thought of you 
more as the solemn moon.

00:10:45.760 --> 00:10:47.830
To me, she's like the sun!

00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:49.280
Um...

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:50.650
That's right!

00:10:51.390 --> 00:10:52.780
Toyokawa-san?

00:10:52.780 --> 00:10:53.860
Hime-chan?

00:10:54.190 --> 00:10:56.870
That bowl we saw in the outlet mall!

00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:02.590
There's absolutely no need to 
think that it doesn't suit you!

00:11:03.210 --> 00:11:05.960
That's why I think you don't 
need to hold yourself back!

00:11:07.710 --> 00:11:09.230
Toyokawa-san...

00:11:10.850 --> 00:11:14.330
I-I'm sorry. I got carried away again.

00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:17.250
Thank you, Toyokawa-san.

00:11:20.630 --> 00:11:22.200
Touko-senpai!

00:11:23.340 --> 00:11:26.640
What's up? You seemed deep in thought.

00:11:30.110 --> 00:11:31.290
I guess...

00:11:32.070 --> 00:11:37.550
I started to lock myself into some 
small place, without even realizing it.

00:11:40.350 --> 00:11:41.740
I see...

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:44.850
I see.

00:11:45.460 --> 00:11:47.110
I'm glad you realized it now!

00:11:48.230 --> 00:11:49.580
Mika-chan...

00:11:54.730 --> 00:11:58.250
<i>I'll do my best and try to 
lift the lid off my heart.</i>

00:11:59.150 --> 00:12:04.090
<i>Because I think my true dreams 
might be locked up in there.</i>

00:12:08.890 --> 00:12:12.620
<i>Touko-senpai got her regular smile back.</i>

00:12:13.280 --> 00:12:17.910
<i>I'm sure she'll make a wonderful 
piece for the cultural festival.</i>

00:12:18.530 --> 00:12:19.920
<i>I can't wait to see it!</i>

00:12:23.210 --> 00:12:26.630
You were brilliant yesterday, Naruse-san.

00:12:26.630 --> 00:12:28.860
Oh, can we just drop that?

00:12:28.860 --> 00:12:31.750
I almost forgot!

00:12:31.750 --> 00:12:33.310
Oh, it's the mysterious tool!

00:12:33.590 --> 00:12:35.530
I don't think I've ever 
seen one of these before.

00:12:35.530 --> 00:12:37.280
What is it, senpai?

00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:40.480
I don't know. This is the first 
time seeing one of these.

00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:42.820
Even President-san doesn't know?

00:12:44.770 --> 00:12:46.660
This is a needle punch.

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:48.200
A Nagoya-style needle punch at that.

00:12:48.420 --> 00:12:50.320
We're in for an expert explanation!

00:12:50.320 --> 00:12:51.650
So what do you use it for?

00:12:51.650 --> 00:12:52.550
Well!

00:12:52.550 --> 00:12:57.700
You use it to pin an eel to the 
board when you cut and clean it.

00:12:58.420 --> 00:13:00.440
Eek...

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:06.040
So it's not a pottery tool!

00:13:06.040 --> 00:13:09.700
Stab, stab, stab, stab, stab.

00:14:25.710 --> 00:14:27.780
We're at the cultural festival 
and he's there, he's there,

00:14:26.550 --> 00:14:35.310
<b>The Mini Mini Pottery Club</b>

00:14:27.780 --> 00:14:30.430
she's there, and she's 
there, and she's there.

00:14:30.430 --> 00:14:33.010
And then, a legend becomes clear.

00:14:33.010 --> 00:14:35.840
Next up, we have 
"Supersized ♥ Cultural Festival"!

00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:39.970
<b>Supersized ♥ Cultural Festival</b>

00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:39.970
<b>Next time:</b>

00:14:35.840 --> 00:14:39.240
Hang in there. I'm sure you can 
spread your wings some day!

00:14:39.970 --> 00:14:41.970
<b></b>
